		<p>
			I am a mathematics Honours student at the Australian National University, supervised by
			Brett Parker. I also learn a great deal from Yixuan Li.
		</p>
		<p>
			I work in symplectic topology. At the moment I study Kirwan maps, which compare the equivariant
			cohomology of a Hamiltonian space with the cohomology of its symplectic quotient. The classical
			theorems are over the rationals. I want to know what still holds over the integers and in Morava
			<i>K</i>-theory.
		</p>

		<h2>Research interests</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Chromatic methods in symplectic topology:</strong> Kirwan maps and their kernels in
				Morava <i>K</i>-theory.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Mirror symmetry:</strong> Teleman’s conjecture on Fukaya categories and Hamiltonian
				reduction.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Quantum cohomology:</strong> quantum Kirwan maps and Gromov–Witten invariants of
				quotients.
			</li>
		</ul>

